  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "The perpendicular segment from point \\(P\\) to line \\(l\\) has length \\(3\\) cm. Could the distance from \\(P\\) to another point \\(Q\\) on \\(l\\) be \\(2\\) cm?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Yes, as long as \\(Q\\) is close enough to the foot of the perpendicular.",
    "B": "No. The perpendicular segment is the shortest, so \\(PQ\\) is at least \\(3\\) cm.",
    "C": "Yes, because \\(PQ\\) is not necessarily longer than the perpendicular segment."
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Among the segments connecting a point outside a line to points on the line, the perpendicular segment is the shortest, so \\(PQ\\) cannot be less than \\(3\\) cm.",
